WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.229
Classic mode gives you four fixed slots.

2
00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:07.023
Graph mode is a node engine with more than fifty node types.

3
00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:09.489
Switch the Modulation section to Graph.

4
00:00:09.944 --> 00:00:15.602
Beginner view looks like the Classic slots, but each row is a real node with a binding.

5
00:00:15.602 --> 00:00:17.944
Click Add patch: an LFO into Z Push.

6
00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:20.019
Change its source to Noise.

7
00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.712
White noise jitters the depth on every frame.

8
00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:26.334
Point it at Rotation instead, and turn the amount up.

9
00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.069
Now the whole raster shivers.

10
00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:29.657
Add a second row.

11
00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:33.583
A Ramp, sweeping H Size from narrow to wide, over and over.

12
00:00:34.037 --> 00:00:36.302
The Library holds ready-made patches.

13
00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.650
Load Getting Started, a slow breathing depth with a note explaining it.

14
00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:46.356
Both mode runs Classic slots and the graph together, so switching never throws your slots away.

15
00:00:46.816 --> 00:00:49.647
Beginner view covers simple one-to-one patches.

16
00:00:49.647 --> 00:00:52.960
Next, the Advanced canvas, where nodes feed each other.
